course: dictionary
lesson: 3438
title: Eyesight: the ability to see
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Eyesight is your ability to see. When people say someone has «good eyesight», they mean that person can see clearly. When someone has «poor eyesight», they find it harder to see things well. Your eyesight is one of the senses you use most every day.
explain: Context helps you work out the meaning. «Ella had an eyesight test and needed new glasses.» Glasses are used to help people see better, so eyesight must be about how well you can see. Try the swap: "Ella had an ability to see test" sounds strange, but the meaning still fits.
explain: Eyesight is an uncountable noun, so we say «good eyesight» or «sharp eyesight», not «a eyesight» or «many eyesights». Other words in the same family, such as «eyesight test», show you what the word is used for.
fact: Eyesight means your ability to see.
fact: «Sharp eyesight» means seeing things very clearly, even from far away.
fact: «Poor eyesight» means finding it hard to see things well.
fact: «Rhinos have poor eyesight but a very good sense of smell and hearing.»
fact: Never look straight at the Sun. «A boy in Arizona looked straight at the Sun during an eclipse; his eyesight was damaged for life.»
exercise: «Ella had an eyesight test and needed new glasses.» What does eyesight mean? | A test for your ears | *Your ability to see | Your favourite colour | A pair of sunglasses
exercise: «Reading in dim light can make eyes tired but doesn't ruin eyesight.» What does this sentence tell you? | Dim light makes you sleepy | Eyes never get tired | *Reading in dim light tires your eyes but does not stop you seeing well | Reading in dim light harms your ability to see for ever
exercise: «Eagles have very sharp eyesight.» What does sharp eyesight suggest? | They cannot see at all | They sleep all day | *They can see very clearly, even from far away | They can smell food from miles away
test: «Rhinos have poor eyesight but a very good sense of smell.» What does poor eyesight mean? | *Finding it harder to see things well | Being unable to see anything at all | A very good sense of smell | Seeing colours brightly
test: Which phrase means you can see well? | Eyes glued shut | *Good eyesight | Eyesight test | Poor eyesight
exam: Which sentence uses eyesight correctly? | The cake was eyesight and sweet | *Her eyesight is good, so she can read the board at the back | The eyesight ran down the hill | Eyesight is a loud noise at night
